Ledger and Ledlight produce the same valued balances.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight aggregate --accounts '*Assets:Investments*' --denominate

========== LEDGER-CLI ==========

ledger --args-only --date-format %Y-%m-%d --no-pager --sort account --exchange USD balance --flat --no-total --format '%20(display_total)  %(account)\n' '^Assets:Investments'

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD

commodity FUND
  format 1000 FUND
account Assets:Investments
account Assets:Cash

P 2024-01-01 FUND 10 USD
P 2024-02-01 FUND 12.5 USD

2024-01-10 Buy fund units
  Assets:Investments  3 FUND {10 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -30 USD

2024-02-15 Buy another unit
  Assets:Investments  1 FUND {12.5 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -12.5 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

           50.00 USD  Assets:Investments
